I believe you are misinterpreting the tinning kit.  This is not the
same as the tin opener (i.e., not used for opening the tins.)
It is a very handy tool which archeologists start off with, which
allow you to preserve the monsters you kill.  If you are sitting
in a pile of dead monsters, and you are already satiated, you can
can them, and save them for later.

On the other hand, at the level character he is playing, he should
have encountered enough soldiers to pick up hordes of C- and
K-rations.  They aren't listed among his props, so we don't know.
If he doesn't have that much of a food supply, he will still want
the tinning kit.


